{"type":"step-attempt","step":"spec-review","sessionId":"640d4223-f044-4e72-9866-5cb6d5906f7d","outcome":{"verdict":"needs-fix","findingsPath":"specrunner/changes/evidence-base/spec-review-result-001.md","error":null,"toolResult":{"ok":true,"approved":true,"findings":[{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"specrunner/changes/evidence-base/spec.md","title":"Req 4 deferral list missing captureHeadSha→null path","rationale":"Spec Requirement 4 enumerates deferral conditions ('non-forward type / unset scopedTestCommand / unavailable runtime / absent base/job-base reference / empty selection') but omits the new path introduced in this change: captureHeadSha returning null → strategy-deferred. Design D4 and Tasks T-03 specify this behavior, but the spec is incomplete as a standalone normative document."},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"specrunner/changes/evidence-base/test-cases.md","title":"TC-014 implementation mechanism not specified","rationale":"TC-014 ('detectBaseImplementationContamination removed with no remaining importers') is categorized as a 'unit' test but the assertion is structural/static (compile-time property). T-06 typecheck green already catches this as a TypeScript compilation error. The test-cases.md does not clarify whether a separate runtime test is needed, risking a redundant grep-based test being added.","line":1},{"severity":"low","resolution":"fixable","file":"specrunner/changes/evidence-base/spec.md","title":"Archive floor fail-closed (absent Evidence Base ref) has no spec scenario","rationale":"Requirement 3 scenario covers only the positive re-run case. The archive floor's fail-closed behavior when synthesizedCommits is empty/absent is specified in design D1 and covered by TC-018, but there is no corresponding normative spec scenario. TC-018 is sourced from tasks/design rather than spec, leaving a minor normative gap."}],"evidence":{"checked":15,"skipped":0,"unverified":2},"observations":[{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/runtime/workspace-materializer.ts","title":"D1 basis verified in both worktree and no-worktree paths","rationale":"Both workspace-materializer.ts (L226-242, worktree path) and local.ts (L429-443, no-worktree path) call appendSynthesizedCommit immediately after the bootstrap commit. The adopt-commits path appends only to the ledger tail. Design D1 claim 'synthesizedCommits[0] is stable across resume/re-run' is structurally correct.","line":226},{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/port/runtime-strategy.ts","title":"captureHeadSha already on port — no new port method needed for candidate resolution","rationale":"captureHeadSha(cwd) exists at L329 of RuntimeStrategy. Design D4 correctly uses this existing method for the green candidate, keeping the port extension minimal (only runTestsOnSynthesizedTree is net-new).","line":329},{"severity":"low","file":"specrunner/changes/evidence-base/design.md","title":"D7 test-file enumeration verified complete","rationale":"All test files listed in D7 (gate.test.ts, gate-empty-selection.test.ts, achieved-assurance.test.ts, 5 tests/unit/core/archive/ files, merge-then-archive-floor-provenance.test.ts, bite-evidence-e2e-gate.test.ts) exist in the repository. The TC-007 disambiguation (non-forward vs strip-test-authority) in gate.test.ts is clearly handled."},{"severity":"low","file":"src/core/step/bite-evidence/oids.ts","title":"resolveBaseCandidateOids candidateOid becomes dead return value post-implementation","rationale":"After the change, the gate no longer reads candidateOid from this function (D3). The return field will remain in the type signature but go unused, which is a minor interface debt. Low risk since the gate fakes and archive floor tests only destructure baseOid from this call.","line":29}]},"followUpAttempts":0,"transientRetryAttempts":0,"addedTurns":{"reportRetry":0,"postWork":0,"outputRepair":0}},"startedAt":"2026-08-14T20:24:09.200Z","endedAt":"2026-08-14T20:33:21.209Z","commitOid":"a8937e64e24ddb414bb097b3